      "blocks": {
        "090a05a9-c530-405c-8480-12d5b201f814": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": false,
            "title": "Which vacuum cleaners are used on construction sites?",
            "text": "<p>A specialist industrial vacuum cleaner called a <a href=\"/collections/dust-extractors\" title=\"Dust Extractors\">dust extractor</a> is used for cleaning potentially harmful dust and dirt on industrial and construction sites. They are graded L, M or H class depending on their use-type.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
            "product_specifications": "",
            "html": "",
            "collection": "",
            "collection_products_per_page": 8,
            "products": [],
            "image_loading": "",
            "video_1": "",
            "video_2": ""
          }
        },
        "entry_RYhhtg": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": false,
            "title": "Do I need to use a dust extractor on a building site?",
            "text": "<p>If you can see dust then you’re probably breathing it in. To keep everyone safe, it’s crucial that your tools are right for the job. Having a vacuum cleaner with a certified level of dust extraction is a vital part of this. It not only keeps you within the law, but also minimises your and your employee's exposure and keeps the potentially harmful dust particles safely contained.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
            "product_specifications": "",
            "html": "",
            "collection": "",
            "collection_products_per_page": 8,
            "products": [],
            "image_loading": "",
            "video_1": "",
            "video_2": ""
          }
        },
        "entry_kf7GKx": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": false,
            "title": "Which features are useful on an industrial vacuum cleaner?",
            "text": "<p>Look for features like high-grade HEPA filtration, integrated power tool take-off sockets, reinforced crush resistant hoses, thick skinned stainless steel tanks and extra long cables.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
            "product_specifications": "",
            "html": "",
            "collection": "",
            "collection_products_per_page": 8,
            "products": [],
            "image_loading": "",
            "video_1": "",
            "video_2": ""
          }
        },
        "entry_cMA6ai": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": false,
            "title": "How do I know the classification of a dust extractor?",
            "text": "<p>L-class and M-class dust extractors that have been certified as meeting HSE standards are easy to spot. The level of classification should be prominently displayed in the form of a sticker attached to the machine. If it doesn't have the sticker and you're in doubt as to whether it's classified or not, contact the the manufacturer.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
            "product_specifications": "",
            "html": "",
            "collection": "",
            "collection_products_per_page": 8,
            "products": [],
